  "_about": {
    "purpose": "Typical adult reference intervals, used ONLY to tell analytes apart when mapping an unknown printed name onto a canonical analyte.",
    "not_for": "Clinical interpretation. A result is flagged normal/low/high strictly from the interval printed on the patient's own report (src/normalize.py), never from this file.",
    "precision_needed": "Order of magnitude. The job is to separate homocysteine (5-15 umol/l) from uric acid (202-417 umol/l), not to decide whether a patient is ill.",
    "provenance": "Seeded from commonly published adult intervals. NOT verified against a Czech clinical source. Before this is relied on beyond a demo it should be checked against CSKB recommendations or a lab handbook, and per-lab or per-doctor overrides added.",
    "units": "Each range is expressed in the analyte's canonical_unit as declared in registry.json.",
    "widened_2026_09_19": "The blood count and differential follow the CHS CLS JEP recommendation for adults (2021); the rest of the additions come from the public reference appendices of EUC Zlin, KNTB Zlin, MZ-Biochem and Skalica (SK), and otherwise from manufacturer inserts as commonly published. Serology indices, qualitative tests, cells normally absent from blood and assay-dependent analytes carry no interval on purpose."
  },
